----- SOURCE CODE
@external(erlang, "one", "two")
@external(webassembly, "gleam:js", "call")
pub fn call(a: Int) -> Int


----- ERROR
error: Invalid WebAssembly module
  ┌─ /src/one/two.gleam:2:1
  │
2 │ @external(webassembly, "gleam:js", "call")
  │ ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

The function `call` has an external WebAssembly implementation in the
module `gleam:js`, which is neither a JavaScript module, ending in `.mjs`
or `.js`, nor a module of the environment, with a plain name like `env`.

Hint: To use another JavaScript module, write a `.mjs` module that
re-exports it.
